-The core data structure is the set of 3D Gaussians. Each Gaussian $g_i$ is defined by:
-*   Mean position $\mu_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$ [G].
-*   Covariance matrix $\Sigma_i \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 3}$, typically parameterized by a rotation matrix $R_i$ (quaternion) and a scaling vector $s_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$ such that $\Sigma_i = R_i S_i S_i^T R_i^T$ where $S_i = \text{diag}(s_i)$ [G].
-*   Opacity $\alpha_i \in [0, 1]$ [G].
-*   Color attributes for view-dependent appearance [S3].
